So matrix multiplication rules: to multiply a 2x2 matrix by a 2x1 matrix, the result will be a 2x1 matrix. Each entry is computed by taking the dot product of the corresponding row of the first matrix with the column of the second matrix.

Let me compute the first entry of the resulting matrix. The first row of the first matrix is [1, 2], and the second matrix's column is [5, 3]. So the dot product is (1)(5) + (2)(3) = 5 + 6 = 11.

Now the second entry of the resulting matrix. The second row of the first matrix is [4, 8]. Dot product with [5, 3] is (4)(5) + (8)(3) = 20 + 24 = 44.

So putting it all together, the product should be:
$$
\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 44 \end{pmatrix}
$$

